@node documenta-cli
@section (documenta cli)

@c %start of fragment

This module defines the command-line interface of the
@command{documenta} program.  See the @ref{CLI} section for additional
information.


@c %end of fragment
This module provides the following interface.


@c %start of fragment

@subsection Procedures
@deffn Procedure call command spec
Call an appropriate procedure for the given command.

@strong{command} (list): A list of strings that represent a command-line
instruction passed to the program (see Guile's command-line procedure).

@strong{spec} (Configuration): A @code{<configuration>} record as
defined by the guile-config library, which specifies the command-line
interface of the program.

@strong{Result}: The @var{command} is followed.  If the command is not
recognized, display help information.

@end deffn


@c %end of fragment

@c %start of fragment

@subsection Variables
@defvar spec
This is a record of the type @code{<configuration>}, which has the
following fields:

@itemize 
@item
@code{name}@item
@code{synopsis}@item
@code{description}@item
@code{wanted}@item
@code{keywords}@item
@code{arguments}@item
@code{subcommands}@item
@code{directory}@item
@code{version}@item
@code{license}@item
@code{copyright}@item
@code{author}@item
@code{parser}@item
@code{alias}@item
@code{generate-help?}@item
@code{generate-usage?}@item
@code{generate-version?}@item
@code{generate-cmdtree?}@end itemize

@end defvar


@c %end of fragment

