@node documenta-commands
@section (documenta commands)

@c %start of fragment

This module defines procedures that are associated to every command
provided by the command-line interface of the @command{documenta}
program.  See the @ref{CLI} and @xref{documenta-cli,(documenta cli)}
sections for additional information.


@c %end of fragment
This module provides the following interface.


@c %start of fragment

@subsection Procedures
@deffn Procedure extract source OPT: destination
Extract the documentation of the library defined in source.

@strong{source} (string): An absolute or relative path to a single Guile
Scheme module file or to a directory containing a collection of modules.
For example: «projects/project-x/libx.scm», «projects/project-z/libz».

@strong{destination} (string): Optional path to a directory where the
final Texinfo files will be saved.  If not provided,
@var{DEFAULT_DOC_PATH} is used (see the module
@ref{documenta-commands}).

@strong{Result}: The API documentation is saved to the @var{destination}
directory.

@end deffn


@c %end of fragment

@c %start of fragment

@subsection Variables
@defvr Variable DEFAULT_DOC_PATH
@verbatim 
"doc/api"
@end verbatim

@end defvr


